      "text": "We are given the line equation defined by points $A(2, 2, 1)$ and $B(5, 1, -2);$\n\\begin{align*}\n&\\vec{U} = (5 - 2)\\mathbf{i} + (1 - 2)\\mathbf{j} + (-2 - 1)\\mathbf{k} = (3)\\mathbf{i} + (-1)\\mathbf{j} + (-3)\\mathbf{k}. \\\\\n\\end{align*}To find a point on the line, compute $t$ of an equation to find $x = 4$:\n\\begin{align*}\n&\\frac{4 - 2}{5 - 2} = \\frac{x - 2}{5 - 2} = \\frac{2}{3} \\\\\n&\\implies 2\\mathbf{i} + (-1)\\mathbf{j} + (-3)\\mathbf{k} = \\mathbf{x} = (4)\\mathbf{i} + (x)\\mathbf{j} + (z)\\mathbf{k} \\\\\n&\\implies x = -1, \\ z = -2.\n\\end{align*}Therefore, the $z$-coordinate of the point is $\\boxed{-2}.$The answer is: -2",
