      "text": "For an arbitrary point on the line, we can use the formula to compute the $x$ and $z$ coordinates of a point on the line as a function of $t$.\nWe have $(x,y,z) = t (3, -1, -3) + (2, 2,1)$.\nTo find $z$ when $x$ is specified, we quotient $3t + 2 = 4$, from which we obtain $t = \\dfrac{2}{3}$.\nThus, $(\\dfrac{2}{3}(3) + 2, -\\dfrac{2}{3}(-1) + 2, -\\dfrac{2}{3}(-3) + 1) = (\\boxed{\\dfrac{16}{3}})$.\n\n[asy]\npair A,B,C,D,[!u=130][:u,2cm,0,90],x;\nB=dir(0);C=B + dir(60);\nD=(2*B + C)/3;\nx=(2*B + 5*D)/7;\ndraw(A--B--C--D--A);\ndraw(D--B);\ndraw(B--(2,0)--C--(2+sqrt(3),sqrt(3))--D--(2-sqrt(3),sqrt(3))--cycle);\ndraw(B..dir(60)..(2+sqrt(3),sqrt(3))--D..dir(240)..(2-sqrt(3),sqrt(3))--cycle);\nlabel(\"A\",A,axes);\nlabel(\"B\",B,axes);\nlabel(\"C\",C,axes);\nlabel(\"D\",D,x);\nlabel(\"C = $3t + 2$\",x);\n[/asy]",
